BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 673 Td (Q1: Why did you use SQLite for vector storage instead of a dedicated vector database like Pinecone or ChromaDB?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 660 Td (Answer: 'For Milestone 1 and prototype deployments, external vector databases introduce) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 648 Td (unnecessary architectural overhead, external service dependencies, network round-trip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 636 Td (latencies \(50-200ms\), and ongoing subscription costs. By serializing 384-dimensional) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 624 Td (float arrays into 1,536-byte raw BLOBs directly within SQLite, we achieve sub-2ms) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 612 Td (dot-product queries via C-optimized NumPy routines, maintain strict ACID transactional) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 600 Td (integrity between document metadata and embeddings, support cascading deletions out of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 588 Td (the box, and make the entire project 100% portable with zero external database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 576 Td (configuration.') Tj ET
BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 556 Td (Q2: Why did you choose Sentence-Transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2 over OpenAI text-embedding-ada-002?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 543 Td (Answer: 'all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is specifically fine-tuned for semantic search and asymmetric) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 531 Td (passage retrieval on 1 billion sentence pairs. It runs entirely on local CPU at ~14,200) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 519 Td (sentences/second with an 80MB footprint, eliminating cloud API costs, privacy leaks of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 507 Td (sensitive healthcare data, and external rate-limit bottlenecks. Its 384 dimensions also) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 495 Td (save 75% memory compared to 1536-D embeddings without sacrificing retrieval precision on) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 483 Td (technical domain queries.') Tj ET
BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 463 Td (Q3: How does your system prevent hallucinations?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 450 Td (Answer: 'Hallucinations in RAG architectures occur when an LLM is fed irrelevant or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 438 Td (low-scoring context passages for out-of-domain queries. We prevent this mathematically) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 426 Td (at the retrieval layer: candidate chunks must exceed a strict 0.35 Cosine Similarity) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 414 Td (cutoff. Queries scoring below this threshold are immediately rejected with an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 402 Td (Unavailable status and zero retrieved passages. Because no irrelevant context is passed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 390 Td (downstream, the model is physically prevented from confabulating answers.') Tj ET
BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 370 Td (Q4: Why is chunk overlap necessary in the sliding-window chunker?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 357 Td (Answer: 'Natural language text often splits core concepts across sentences. If text is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 345 Td (cut strictly at character 500 without overlap, a critical definition or conditional) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 333 Td (clause might be bifurcated, causing neither chunk to contain sufficient semantic context) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 321 Td (to match a user query. Our 100-character \(20%\) sliding overlap ensures that boundary) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 309 Td (concepts are redundantly preserved across consecutive chunks, significantly boosting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 297 Td (Top-1 retrieval recall.') Tj ET
BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 277 Td (Q5: How do you handle duplicate file uploads?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 264 Td (Answer: 'During upload, the backend computes a cryptographic SHA-256 hash of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 252 Td (incoming byte stream before parsing. The database checks this hash against the UNIQUE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 240 Td (file_hash index in the documents table. If a duplicate is detected, the upload pipeline) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 228 Td (terminates early, returning the existing document ID and status with is_duplicate: true,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 216 Td (preventing duplicate chunks and vector bloat.') Tj ET
BT 0.2 0.3 0.45 rg /F2 9 Tf 50 196 Td (Q6: How are tabular formats like CSV handled semantically?) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 183 Td (Answer: 'Raw CSV rows lack sentence structure. Our extractor transposes each tabular) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 171 Td (record into key-value pairs formatted as: Record N: Header1: Value1, Header2: Value2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 159 Td (This provides rich context for Sentence-Transformers to encode both the column semantics) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 147 Td (and the cell data, allowing comparative queries \(e.g., vital signs across patient age) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 135 Td (groups\) to match accurately.') Tj ET
